    "candidate_assumptions": [
      {
        "source": "Euclidean d-dimensional source beta1/alpha=kappa^-1 and 0<eta<=1; exact argmin and Gaussian gradient definition.",
        "lean": "Source beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2 <= D2V(x)[v,v] <= normv^2 for every x,v.\nFinite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; arbitrary measurable parameter space S; actual measurable eta:S->R and y:S->E with 0<eta(s)<=1 for every s. These coordinate-free/parameter-space extensions are disclosed.\nNo supplied proximal point, minimizer, measurable selector, gradient estimate, Lipschitz bound or Markov kernel. All are produced from the literal potential and actual Gaussian pushforward. The source numerical-prox call cap eta<=1/(2beta) remains a separate computational contract."
      },
      {
        "source": "Actual proximal existence/uniqueness/optimality are implicit and source uses fixed-eta nonexpansivity.",
        "lean": "The constructed uniform damped fixed point supplies measurable selector, true equation and unique quadratic minimum internally."
      },
      {
        "source": "Gaussian estimator (3.2), only input Lipschitz (4.4) and noise Lipschitz (4.5).",
        "lean": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the genuine quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and fixed-eta nonexpansivity. The literal Gaussian gradient evaluator G(s,z)=gradientV(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*z) is jointly measurable and obeys input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta for equal eta. Produce an actual Markov kernel K(s)=stdGaussian.map(G(s,-)). This covers the exact evaluator (3.2) and only Lemma4.2 (4.4)-(4.5), with no posterior or finite-query claim."
      },
      {
        "source": "Separate bias/MGF, posterior standardized law, Wp, warmness, numerical implementation, both main theorems and composition.",
        "lean": "Source beta1 alpha=kappainv kappa>=1 and0<eta<=1, genuine C2/global allpoint-allvector Hessian. Full-space finite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurable parameter spaces are disclosed representation extensions. Actual selector/gradient/kernel witnesses are outputs, never input certificates. Exact Gaussian gradient-output kernel is not RGO posterior or HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Old eta<=1/2 construct remains preserved. Numericalprox calls sourceeta<=1/(2beta) do not grant fullrange finite-query work. No standardized affine posterior law or position moment, history-integrated moment, bias4.2/GaussianMGF4.3/fullLemma4.2/Wp/higher smoothing/sampler/initialization/main/querycost/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost."
      }
    ]
